# Version and changelog

Whenever you modify application code in this project, finish the task by updating the version and changelog.

## Version (`app/build.gradle.kts`)

- Increment `versionCode` by 1 on every release-worthy change.
- Update `versionName` using semantic versioning:
  - **Patch** (1.3.0 → 1.3.1): bug fixes only
  - **Minor** (1.3.0 → 1.4.0): new features or behaviour changes
  - **Major**: breaking changes (rare for this app)
- The UI reads `BuildConfig.VERSION_NAME` automatically — do not hardcode version strings elsewhere.

## Changelog (`CHANGELOG.md`)

- Add a new `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section at the top (below the intro), following [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/) format.
- Group entries under `### Added`, `### Changed`, and `### Fixed` as appropriate.
- Write user-facing descriptions of what changed and why it matters — not internal refactors unless they affect behaviour.
- One changelog entry per version bump; include all changes made in that session or since the last version.

## When to skip

- Do not bump version for documentation-only edits, comment-only changes, or build/IDE config that does not affect the shipped app — unless the user explicitly asks to version those changes.
